From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 05 Nov 2026 22:43:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep RTNL across the WED reset wait

An ethernet reset calls the WED reset callback under RTNL. The
callback requests an L1 recovery, releases RTNL and waits until the
recovery stops DMA. A task that waits for RTNL, such as a read of
ethtool statistics, can take it then. That task blocks on the device
mutex, which the recovery holds, and the recovery waits for the
ethernet reset, which waits for RTNL. After its limit of 3 seconds,
the recovery restarts WED. The frame engine reset that follows clears
the WDMA rings, and stations drop and cannot associate again.

Keep RTNL for the wait. The recovery takes no RTNL, and a task that
needs both locks waits for RTNL first.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mmio.c |    5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/mmio.c
+++ b/mt7996/mmio.c
@@ -523,12 +523,13 @@ static int mt7996_mmio_wed_reset(struct
 	if (ret)
 		goto out;
 
-	rtnl_unlock();
+	/* RTNL stays held: a task that takes it during the wait can block on
+	 * the device mutex of the recovery, which waits for the caller
+	 */
 	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&mdev->mmio.wed_reset, 20 * HZ)) {
 		dev_err(mdev->dev, "wed reset timeout\n");
 		ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
-	rtnl_lock();
 out:
 	clear_bit(MT76_STATE_WED_RESET, &mphy->state);
 
